# ==========================================
weights/
temp-tf-models/
*.onnx
*.h5
*.keras
*.ckpt
*.pb
*.pt
*.pth
*.tflite
*.safetensors

# ==========================================
# KERAS AND MACHINE LEARNING CACHES
# ==========================================
.keras/
wandb/
mlruns/
lightning_logs/

# ==========================================
# GENERATED FEATURES AND EXPERIMENT OUTPUTS
# ==========================================
data/results/
data/recordings/*.npy
data/recordings/*predictions*.csv
data/processed/
outputs/
logs/
*.log

# ==========================================
# AUDIO RECORDINGS
# ==========================================
data/recordings/*.wav
data/recordings/*.mp3
data/recordings/*.flac

# ==========================================
# LOCAL EDITOR AND OPERATING SYSTEM FILES
# ==========================================
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ==========================================
# TEMPORARY FILES
# ==========================================
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
```

## What this configuration does

| Component | GitHub |
|---|---|
| Backend Python code | <badge color="success">Included</badge> |
| Frontend application | <badge color="success">Included</badge> |
| Evaluation scripts | <badge color="success">Included</badge> |
| Test cases | <badge color="success">Included</badge> |
| README and documentation | <badge color="success">Included</badge> |
| Dataset files (except excluded paths) | <badge color="success">Included</badge> |
| Model weights | <badge color="danger">Excluded</badge> |
| Audio recordings | <badge color="danger">Excluded</badge> |
| Virtual environment | <badge color="danger">Excluded</badge> |
| API keys and secrets | <badge color="danger">Excluded</badge> |

**Important:** This configuration excludes all `.pt`, `.pth`, `.onnx`, `.h5`, and similar model files throughout the repository. If you have small pretrained models that should be included, we can selectively allow them.

## Now push your project to GitHub

Run these commands one by one in your VS Code terminal:

```bash
git status
```

```bash
git add -A
```

```bash
git commit -m "Update Bioacoustic Trimodal AI project"
```

```bash
git branch -M main
```

```bash
git remote -v
```

If no remote exists:

```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/mahesh-gaikwad507/bioacoustic-trimodal.git
```

Finally:

```bash
git push -u origin main
```

**Note:** If your GitHub repository already contains commits, you may need to pull and reconcile its history before pushing. Also, `.gitignore` does not remove files that Git is already tracking.

